.TH mnnn-pipeline 1  "mnnn-pipeline 2.15.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-pipeline \- Pipelines: saved, named graphs (DAGs) of sources, code spaces, views and filters that end in model tables. Create, edit, show, run, export and import them
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn pipeline\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pipelines: saved, named graphs (DAGs) of sources, code spaces, views and filters that end in model tables. Create, edit, show, run, export and import them
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-create(1)
A new pipeline
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-edit(1)
Change a pipeline (a new version): add or replace nodes and edges, remove nodes
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-show(1)
The graph, in order, with what is wrong with it
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-list(1)
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-run(1)
Run it: code spaces are approved first; `\-` feeds standard input to `\-` sources
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-remove(1)
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-approve(1)
Approve a draft (a pipeline from a peer) so it can run; its code is approved on run
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-export(1)
Write a pipeline file: nodes, edges, code (by trust hash), sink models by name
.TP
mnnn\-pipeline\-import(1)
Import a pipeline file: shows the plan, then asks
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.15.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
